# GlassWave Firebase configuration
#
# The web app already ships with the official `glasswave-4f5da` project
# (Email/Password sign-in). Leave these unset unless you intentionally want
# a fork or staging build to talk to a *different* Firebase project.
#
# A stale / demo / wrong-project config is the usual reason the app reports
# `auth/operation-not-allowed` even though Email/Password is enabled on
# glasswave-4f5da. If you override, every value must belong to the same project.
#
# Official defaults (used when unset):
#   VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyCmRLbOBFhshcFmKmmmCCRUsQVwQ2iFCW4
#   VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=glasswave-4f5da.firebaseapp.com
#   VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=glasswave-4f5da
#   VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=glasswave-4f5da.firebasestorage.app
#   VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=62843359036
#   VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:62843359036:web:82aa269d0c9bc0e78d9839
#
# Optional: attach the Auth emulator. Do NOT set this unless the emulator is
# running — otherwise the client talks to a local project with Email/Password
# typically disabled.
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR=http://127.0.0.1:9099
#
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
